import LeanFM.LLMGenerated.SelfHosting
import LeanFM.ChatUI.Implementation

/-! Implementation mapping for the `selfhost.session.*` requirements: the session-type library in
LeanFM/Session/. These clauses were written on 2026-11-07 from the code and tests that already
existed, so the mapping records what the library does rather than a plan. Tests named here are
`#guard`s in modules built with the library (LeanFM.Session imports them), so `lake build` runs
them. -/

namespace LeanFM.LLMGenerated.SessionImplementation
open LeanFM.ChatUI.Implementation
open LeanFM.LLMGenerated.SelfHosting

def decisions : List ImplementationDecision :=
  [ decision "session-syntax"
      ["clause:selfhost.session.syntax"]
      ["LeanFM/Session/Syntax.lean", "LeanFM/Session/Global.lean"]
      "The protocol command is a Lean syntax extension in LeanFM.Session.Syntax. protocol Name (R1, ..., Rn) { statements } defines Name : R -> ... -> R -> Global R. Each statement elaborates to one Global constructor: msg (an Interaction with id, label, src, dst, cause and guard), act, choice, par, join, loop and var (rec and continue; continue ends its branch), sessions, and andThen for include. A label is a type, referred to as Option Label; the command declares an empty structure for a label that resolves to no constant (decision session-lean-syntax). cause, route (a string literal) and status (a numeral) fill Interaction.cause, route and status; no rule reads route or status. A where clause becomes a Guard holding its text, beside an unused let that type-checks it as a Lean proposition over the payload types of the ids it mentions, which must be message ids bound earlier or the guarded message itself; conformance runs the text with Session.Where."
      ["LeanFM/Session/SessionTests.lean: Purchase elaborates with its labels in order; the where clause keeps its text p.amount = q.price", "LeanFM/Session/LeanSyntaxTests.lean: a condition naming a missing field or an unbound id is an elaboration error"]
  , decision "session-choice"
      ["clause:selfhost.session.choice"]
      ["LeanFM/Session/Global.lean"]
      "Global.decider takes the first steps of the branches that do something (Global.first): a message's sender or an event's role; empty branches are ignored. One role starting them all is the decider; several roles give 'no single role decides a choice, so it is a race: ' naming who starts what; no branch doing anything is also an error. choiceIssues reports the decider's error, or 'C's choice: two branches start with the same event' when first events repeat, and recurses into branches, par, join, loops and sessions. classicChoiceIssues keeps the classic sender-only rule for comparison."
      ["LeanFM/Session/SessionTests.lean: TransferWithTimer reports the race between Sender's Timeout and Receiver's Ack; Transfer, where the receiver decides, has no issues"]
  , decision "session-causes"
      ["clause:selfhost.session.causes"]
      ["LeanFM/Session/Global.lean"]
      "Global.causeIssues walks every linear run (Global.runs) and reports a message whose cause names a message its sender has neither sent nor received earlier on that run."
      ["LeanFM/Session/SessionTests.lean: a Paid from the bank caused by an Order the bank never saw is reported (Paid: Bank never saw o); Purchase has no cause issues"]
  , decision "session-projection"
      ["clause:selfhost.session.projection"]
      ["LeanFM/Session/Global.lean"]
      "Global.project first looks for a service: Global.nestedSessions lists the bodies of the sessions blocks nested directly in the protocol's body and Global.withoutNested removes them; a role involved in some nested body but not in the rest is projected on each such body and served, one body as sessions { l } and several as sessions { offer } when their Local.firstReceives are present and disjoint, otherwise an error naming the role. Other roles are projected by projectFrom as before. Global.project r runs projectFrom r started: a role not involved in what follows projects to done; a message becomes send or recv or disappears; an event becomes act at its role; a choice the role decides becomes select, and any other becomes mergeBranches. mergeBranches flattens nested offers and accepts, as an offer, branches whose first receivable messages (Local.firstReceives, which looks inside par) are non-empty and pairwise disjoint, provided the role has not started or is present in every branch; a role that has not started may be absent from branches; otherwise branches that begin with the same received label must continue alike. Anything else fails with 'R cannot tell which branch C chose' (with 'after L' when two branches share their first label). sessions projects its body with started false. Global.issues collects choice, cause and projection failures for the listed roles."
      ["LeanFM/Session/SessionTests.lean: Purchase projects for the shop as select and for the bank as an offer with an empty branch; PurchaseWithHold reports that the bank cannot tell which branch the shop chose", "LeanFM/Session/ProjectionTests.lean: a client that has paid tells branches apart when one answers inside a par or after one; a declined branch that tells the client nothing is still rejected", "LeanFM/SessionToolsTests.lean: the two-factor login example checks clean over HTTP with notHttp for the text message; Sms projects to a service serving SendCode, Queued, Text while Auth keeps the nested sessions in place; written inline, Sms cannot tell which branch was chosen; a mailer serving two kinds of session gets an offer, and two kinds starting alike are reported; simulated logins with their text-message sessions conform, and a text session skipping the answer does not; the generated Sms starts each session at SmsS1; dropping the gateway answer is incompatible with the old version"]
  , decision "session-composition"
      ["clause:selfhost.session.composition"]
      ["LeanFM/Session/Global.lean", "LeanFM/Session/Syntax.lean"]
      "include P roles elaborates to Global.andThen (P roles) rest, so the included protocol's done continues with the rest. par branches k and join n branches k carry their continuation k; Global.runs interleaves nothing and lists branches in order for linear checks, while projection keeps par. sessions body k serves copies of body beside k. No construct cancels a branch."
      ["LeanFM/Session/SessionTests.lean: ReplicatedOrder includes a 2-of-3 Replicate join, has no issues, and has 8 labels"]
  , decision "session-http"
      ["clause:selfhost.session.http"]
      ["LeanFM/Session/Http.lean"]
      "Global.replay walks one run on the HTTP channels and returns the requests still pending at its end with the cuts found; httpCutsStreaming reports the cuts of every run and, over Global.finishedRuns (runs that reach the end without going round a loop again), each request left without a response. Global.httpCutsStreaming g isHttp mayCall streams keeps, along each run, the pending requests (id, caller, callee). A message on an HTTP channel whose cause chain reaches a pending request made by its receiver to its sender is that request's response (the request stays pending when the pair streams); otherwise it is a new request, and is a cut unless mayCall holds. A response that goes to anyone but the caller is reported as 'L answers P, which C sent to S, but goes to D'; an uncallable request as 'L is a request from S to D, which S may not call'. httpCuts is the non-streaming case."
      ["LeanFM/Session/SessionTests.lean: Purchase over HTTP reports Paid going to the shop instead of the client and Shipped as an uncallable request, and Pay, Paid and Shipped left without a response; PurchaseHttp has no cuts", "LeanFM/SessionToolsTests.lean: the first draft of two-factor login reports the code request as never answered; a request answered after a loop is not reported; a text message is an uncallable, unanswered request until notHttp names its channel; a malformed notHttp is rejected"]
  , decision "session-physics"
      ["clause:selfhost.session.physics"]
      ["LeanFM/Session/Physics.lean", "LeanFM/Session/Spec.lean"]
      "Channel has capacity, whenFull, order, sharding, loss, duplication, masked and extra; Channel.conditions derives the surfaced conditions (loss from loss or dropping, reorder from any order, duplicate, per-key order from sharding, reject from rejecting, plus extra) minus masked. Presets: reliable, udp, stream, http, kafka. Physics.channel returns reliable for an undeclared pair; Physics.used lists the channels a protocol uses with their conditions. Spec bundles the protocol, roles, physics, handled conditions per channel, CTL properties over message atoms and assumptions; Spec.issues reports the core rules' issues, unknown atoms, and every surfaced condition of a used channel that its protocol does not handle."
      ["LeanFM/Session/SessionTests.lean: TFTP over UDP reports that the Receiver to Sender channel surfaces reorder, which its protocol does not handle; with no physics declared there is nothing to handle"]
  , decision "session-topology"
      ["clause:selfhost.session.topology"]
      ["LeanFM/Session/Topology.lean"]
      "IfaceKind is a channel plus a lineage; refine adds and removes conditions and extends the lineage. Kinds: call, queue, stream, http, api, ingressHttp, ingressHttps, datagram, topic. Iface has a scope (ingress, peering, internal, local), a name and a kind. The tree's nodes are actors with interfaces and groups placed as outside, island, datacenter, machine, replicated or sharded. Placed.implicitName joins island, actor, scope and interface. Topology.reachable applies the scope rules from the common prefix of the two paths; Topology.channel adds partition across islands, hostile from or to outside, reject into a replicated group and per-key order into a shard."
      ["LeanFM/Session/SessionTests.lean: us.Shop.ingress.https is found; the bank's internal API is unreachable from the outside client and reachable from the shop; that channel surfaces duplicate, reject, close and timeout; a grpc kind refined from http has lineage stream, http"]
  , decision "session-diagram"
      ["clause:selfhost.session.diagram"]
      ["LeanFM/Session/Diagram.lean"]
      "Global.diagram g roles theme title walks g once in a state monad holding the vertical cursor, the SVG elements and the ids of messages drawn so far with their sender, receiver, cause and whether each was a reply. Arrows are emitted only from msg; isReply walks the cause chain (at most 64 links) and a message reaching a drawn non-reply message from its receiver to its sender gets class msg reply and a dashed stroke. The where clause is a separate text of class guard under the arrow. A frame opening directly under another frame's tab starts lower so the tabs do not overlap. The label adds ' - route' and ' - status'. answers returns the request a reply answers; a request with an id opens an activation bar (request id, callee, inset = the callee's bars still open, top, bottom), its first reply closes it. A later reply extends the most recent segment when no divider follows its bottom; otherwise it adds a segment starting at the greater of branchTop and the previous segment top. This prevents repeated replies from creating a bar at the initial branchTop of zero or before their request. Bars are drawn under the arrows. act emits an action box. choice, par, join, loop, sessions and box each emit a frame (class frame alt, par, join, loop, sessions, ref) with a UML tab (alt, par, loop, ref) and a caption: the decider from Global.decider as 'R decides', or 'race: no single role decides'; 'any k of n'; the loop name; the included protocol's name. Branches are separated by dashed dividers; nested frames are inset. var emits 'continue N'. Every piece of protocol text passes through diagramEscape. Themes: dark (the default, a #111 background) and light. Arrows are drawn at Shape.arrowWidth (2.5) with arrowheads in user-space units; frameTop moves 14 below the last arrow (22 below a frame tab) and dividers and frame bottoms 12, so no frame edge or divider runs along an arrow. Diagram.columnWidth sizes the lifeline spacing from the longest Diagram.labelText among Diagram.messagesOf the protocol; a choice's caption is the decider Global.decider names."
      ["LeanFM/Session/SessionTests.lean: in the diagrams of Purchase, Checkout, Transfer and ReplicatedOrder every arrow is at least 6 pixels from every frame edge and divider; messages are drawn at stroke width 2.5 with arrowheads in user-space units", "LeanFM/Session/SessionTests.lean: Purchase draws one arrow per label, two dashed replies (Quote, SoldOut) and one alt frame captioned Shop decides, with the guard after Pay; ReplicatedOrder draws a ref frame for Replicate around a join frame captioned any 2 of 3; Transfer draws a loop frame with continue Block; TransferWithTimer draws an action box and a race caption; a sessions block draws a sessions frame; PayThenCharge draws Quote, Hold and Receipt as replies and Order, Pay and Verify as calls; a guard with <, && and > is escaped and no raw < from it appears; RepeatedReplies draws one activation from its request through both replies and no header overlap; Checkout shows - POST /orders, - 201 and - 402 in labels and draws six activation bars; a route with <, & and > is escaped"]
  , decision "session-calls"
      ["clause:selfhost.session.calls"]
      ["LeanFM/Session/Calls.lean"]
      "Global.messages lists every message once in written order (a choice copies its continuation into each branch, so a message is kept at its first appearance, keyed by id, label, roles and cause). Global.classify folds over them: a message answers the first request up its cause chain (at most 64 links) whose sender is its receiver and whose receiver is its sender. Calls.inDetail r m walks m's ancestors and is true when it meets r before any of r's responses; Calls.parent m is the nearest ancestor request whose detail holds m; Global.calls builds the tree from requests by parent; callsText prints two lines per call, 'id: Label  Src -> Dst  route' then '  returns R1 status | R2 status' (or 'returns no reply'), nested calls indented four spaces. Local.typestate walks the projection in StateM, allocating S0, S1, ... in order and printing methods per state (send as sendLabel(m : Label) : Next, receive as receive() : Label times Next, events as Label() : Next, offer as one receive with alternatives, par as fork, sessions as serve, a branch that does nothing as stop() : End); Typestate.norm turns a par with one live side into that side followed by the continuation. Global.typestates projects each listed role and returns its typestate or the projection error."
      ["LeanFM/Session/SessionTests.lean: Checkout lists two calls with routes and statuses and the bank's charge nested under the payment; Purchase lists Pay and Shipped with no reply and Paid nested under Pay; the client's and the bank's typestates of Checkout and the sender's of Transfer (continue returns to S0) are exact"]
  , decision "session-generative"
      ["clause:selfhost.session.generative", "clause:selfhost.session.generative.execution", "clause:selfhost.session.generative.monitor"]
      ["LeanFM/Session/GenerativeTypes.lean", "LeanFM/Session/Text.lean", "LeanFM/Session/Generative.lean", "LeanFM/SessionTools.lean", "LeanFM/MCP.lean", "LeanFM/SessionView.html"]
      "Extend the read-only protocol parser with annotation AST nodes and retain a core-erasing build. Store the original body beside Global in parsed tool protocols. Resolve inline and external annotations by unique named choices and message id (or unambiguous label); external entries replace matching inline entries explicitly and identify their origin. Use exact rational arithmetic, milliseconds and bounded finite path expansion (4096 paths, 200 statements, 16 distribution entries, existing 64 KiB and nesting bounds). Validate each path's clock/event scope and time monotonicity before sampling. Seeded selection draws integer tickets against exact common denominators. Emit ordinary Session.Event envelopes and separate obligation reports. Timed log monitoring replays timestamped prefixes against structural paths without requiring their sampled delay or probability. Check all annotations independently of Global.issues; preserve existing unannotated simulation and JSON protocols. No filesystem, network, external code execution, or credentials in this layer. Reject unsupported timed concurrency/recursion/includes with actionable errors. Exact distributions and stable metadata are returned as data, not inserted as HTML. The session view displays effective annotations and deadline reports through text nodes and retains the external overlay in editor calls."
      ["LeanFM/Session/GenerativeTests.lean: accepted example, erasure, external overlay equivalence/replacement, exact mass, deterministic generation and conform round trip; zero-weight branch retained; invalid fractions, sums, bounds, forward refs, duplicate ids, unsupported scheduling and backwards times rejected; deadline boundary, late, pending, missing times, wrong sender and separate sessions checked", "LeanFM/MCPTests.lean: session tools expose overlay and horizon arguments through MCP"]
  , decision "session-mdp"
      ["clause:selfhost.session.mdp"]
      ["LeanFM/Session/Generative.lean", "LeanFM/Session/Decision.lean", "LeanFM/SessionTools.lean", "LeanFM/MCP.lean", "LeanFM/SessionView.lean", "LeanFM/SessionView.html"]
      "Retain decision markers and sampled local weights during finite path expansion; schedule ignores markers. Build a prefix tree with explicit choice/action nodes, event/time state nodes and terminal reports. Preserve complete action/event identity in keys, rather than labels alone. Multiply local exact weights and verify against compiled path masses, then check the sum of unique terminal masses equals one and each nonterminal outgoing distribution equals one. Bound graphs to 96 nodes and dimensions/output to explicit limits. Sum violating terminal masses once regardless of obligation count. Generate DiagramModel shapes and SVG through the existing escaped renderer; the MCP view builds SVG and text nodes, never inserts returned markup. session_mdp uses ordinary tool dispatch and session view attachment, returns the original overlay and DesiredOutput provenance, and refuses unresolved policies or unsupported timed scheduling."
      ["LeanFM/Session/DecisionTests.lean: exact example masses and total, external replacement, zero branches, unknown weights, duplicate labels, multiple obligations, pending status, nesting, resource limits and SVG injection", "LeanFM/MCPTests.lean and scripts/session_view_smoke.js: discovery, dispatch, SVG/shapes and native view rendering with overlay retention"]
  , decision "session-amounts"
      ["clause:selfhost.session.amounts"]
      ["LeanFM/Session/GenerativeTypes.lean", "LeanFM/Session/Text.lean", "LeanFM/Session/Generative.lean", "LeanFM/Session/Decision.lean", "LeanFM/SessionTools.lean"]
      "GenerativeTypes adds Amount (unit and a list of quantity and probability outcomes) and Penalty (quantity, unit, payee) on Obligation. Text parses amount after status (one quantity, or sample of quantity-unit-probability entries checked by checkWeights, one unit, distinct quantities) into Stmt.valued, which build erases to its message like Stmt.timed, and pays N UNIT to Role after on breach record. Generative.expandStmt turns valued into one Action.transfer per outcome after the message action (sender, receiver, unit, quantity, weight), multiplying the path probability; timed keeps the actions after its message and multiplies too, so amount and time samples compose in either nesting. resolveStmt records amount metadata. schedule ignores transfers. Decision.steps folds a transfer into the preceding state step (key and detail carry the amount, weight multiplied) and gives the terminal its balances: per role and unit, received minus sent, plus each violated obligation's penalty, held as signed integers. Decision.expected sums terminal mass times balance with exact rationals kept as separate credit and debit masses, written with a sign. session_mdp returns balances per terminal, expectedBalances and expectedPenalty."
      ["LeanFM/Session/DecisionTests.lean: the priced deposit example gives exact terminal balances, conserved per unit, expected balances and expected penalty; amount samples multiply terminal masses and compose with time samples; erasure keeps the Global unchanged; invalid amounts (mixed units, bad sums, duplicate quantities, oversized, amount on an event, penalty to self or to an unknown role) are rejected; a pending obligation's penalty is not counted"]
  , decision "session-mdp-loops"
      ["clause:selfhost.session.mdp.loops"]
      ["LeanFM/Session/Chain.lean", "LeanFM/Session/Decision.lean", "LeanFM/SessionTools.lean", "LeanFM/MCP.lean", "LeanFM/SessionView.html"]
      "Chain.build walks the resolved statement list backwards with a continuation state, in a state monad holding states and edges: a message, with its amount and time annotations peeled, adds a state whose one edge to the continuation carries the message, probability 1 and the amount's mean as an exact Rat; an event likewise; a weighted choice adds a choice state with one policy edge per branch to that branch's entry; rec allocates its state first, builds the body with the loop name bound to it and the rec's continuation, and adds a loop edge to the body's entry; continue returns the bound state; a clock is skipped; an obligation, par, join, sessions, include or unweighted choice is rejected. The end state is absorbing. Chain.solve builds (I - Q)^T over the transient states and solves for the start's unit vector by Gauss-Jordan elimination with exact Rat; a zero pivot means a closed set of transient states and is reported as a session that can loop forever. Traversals, balances and expected messages are sums over edges. The drawing lays states out in levels by breadth-first depth from the start; forward edges are straight arrows, edges back to a state no deeper than their source are curves to the right; edge labels sit on background plates. Decision draws a transfer on the edge into its message's state rather than in the state, and shows each non-terminal node's mass as its expected visits. session_mdp chooses the chain when the body contains rec or view is chain, and the tree otherwise."
      ["LeanFM/Session/ChainTests.lean: a retry loop gives exact visits, traversals and expected balances; a geometric loop with exit probability 1/4 visits its state 4 times; the priced example without its obligation gives the tree's expected balances; a loop with no way out, an obligation in a loop, par, an unweighted choice and too many states are rejected; the SVG escapes protocol text and draws back edges as paths"]
  , decision "session-mdp-rewards"
      ["clause:selfhost.session.mdp.rewards"]
      ["LeanFM/Session/GenerativeTypes.lean", "LeanFM/Session/Text.lean", "LeanFM/Session/Generative.lean", "LeanFM/Session/Chain.lean", "LeanFM/SessionTools.lean"]
      "TimeExpr gains relative (after), which schedule bases on the previous event's time and Text writes back as after. Accrual (payer, payee, unit, quantity, periodMs) is a Stmt that build erases and expandStmt refuses with a pointer to the chain view. Chain.build gives every message and event edge the mean of its relative delay (an absolute time is noted when no accrual is present and refused when one is) and turns accrue into a zero-delay rate edge. Chain.regimes propagates the accruals in force from the start along edges in breadth-first order (a rate edge replaces the accrual with the same payer, payee and unit) and refuses a state reached with two different sets. Each edge into the single end is retargeted to an end state of its own, named after the edge, so outcomes stay apart. Chain.solveAbsorb solves (I - Q) h = r for each end with the same exact Gauss-Jordan elimination, giving the probability of each outcome from every state. An outcome's joint expectation of an edge reward is visits(src) x p x reward x h(dst); dividing by the outcome's probability gives the conditional value. Expected time, residence and accrued amounts are sums over edges of traversals x mean delay (x rate). session_mdp picks the chain when the body has rec or accrue. Chain.contributions sums traversals x amount per role, unit and source in protocol order; Chain.legend writes each role's units with their sources and, for exactly two units of opposite sign, the larger magnitude per the smaller; Chain.breakdownJson nests them exactly."
      ["LeanFM/Session/ChainTests.lean: a loan with a two-week grace at 0 USD per week and 10 USD per week after gives exact expected duration, interest and balances; per-outcome probabilities sum to 1 and conditional balances average back to the overall ones; the limit order splits into Filled and GaveUp outcomes of 1/2 each with 1004 and 4 USD; after delays drive the tree's times too; a rate that differs between merging paths, an absolute time with an accrual, an accrual in the tree view, a zero period, a rate to oneself and a negative rate are rejected"]
  , decision "session-mdp-walk"
      ["clause:selfhost.session.mdp.walk"]
      ["LeanFM/Session/Chain.lean", "LeanFM/SessionTools.lean", "LeanFM/MCP.lean"]
      "Chain.walk keeps the current state and, for each step, searches breadth-first through choice, loop and rate edges (each state once) for message or event edges matching the step's label and, when given, sender and receiver; exactly one match is taken, with the path of silent edges to it, and the product of their probabilities. Counts per edge, visits per state and the time per state (the step's afterMs, or the edge's mean delay) accumulate as exact rationals; rewards apply the same per-traversal function as expectations (the trade vector, and each rate in force at the edge's source times the step's time). session_mdp with an events argument groups the stream by session (first appearance), turns timeMs or time into delays since the previous event of the session, walks each session and sums their balances, durations and counts; a walk argument walks one hand-written list. The result replaces expectations, and the report says these are realized values of the given walks."
      ["LeanFM/Session/ChainTests.lean: a limit-order walk that is rejected once and then fills pays 4 USD in fees and 1000 for 10 shares, with probability 1/32; a loan stream with actual times gives the interest for exactly the time spent; two sessions sum; an unmatched step, an ambiguous step, a time that goes backwards and too many events are rejected"]
  , decision "session-mdp-horizon"
      ["clause:selfhost.session.mdp.horizon"]
      ["LeanFM/Session/GenerativeTypes.lean", "LeanFM/Session/Text.lean", "LeanFM/Session/Generative.lean", "LeanFM/Session/Chain.lean", "LeanFM/SessionTools.lean", "LeanFM/MCP.lean"]
      "TimeExpr gains period (at next d); schedule places a gated step at (now / d + 1) * d; Text writes it back as at next. Chain edges keep their largest delay and their gate period. Chain.horizon finds the one gate edge g, refuses a cycle among the other edges reachable from the start (depth-first with colours) and a longest path over them, start to g's source or g's target back to it, longer than the period. It solves two absorbing chains with g's source added to the ends, from the start and from g's target, takes q0 and q from their visits at g's source, sums the geometric series exactly with Rat, combines visits as v_init + C v_cycle with C = q0 S(N-1) and sets g's source to the passages q0 S(N); the wait is P x passages minus the joint expected work time to the gate (visits x probability x delay x the probability of reaching the gate from the edge's target), and g's delay becomes the mean wait, so expected, residence, duration and the drawing apply unchanged. session_mdp with horizon parses it as a duration and returns periods, stillRunning, totals and the drawing."
      ["LeanFM/Session/ChainTests.lean: weekly rent that always continues passes the gate exactly 52 times in 52 weeks, 52000 USD and 52 roomweeks, duration exactly 52 weeks; with a 1/4 chance of notice each week, 4 weeks give 175/64 rents; a loop around the gate, work longer than the period, two gates, a gate without a horizon in the chain and a horizon shorter than a period are rejected; the tree times a gated step at the period boundary"]
