      "Sla.Execution holds the events in a Std.HashMap keyed by timestamp, the timestamps in order, a forward index (children by cause and prev) and the sparse reward map. causalPast walks prev and cause backwards; view is the union of the causal pasts of the role's own events; rewardAt walks prev backwards from the event to the first timestamp in the reward map and returns that vector (the zero vector when the chain starts without one); Execution.make refuses a reward vector equal to the one it would inherit through prev. observe takes each entry, walks its causal future forwards (only events up to the deadline), and records hit, miss or pending (deadline after the last timestamp). Windows group entries by floor(ts / W) or in consecutive blocks of N; a window is closed when the last timestamp is at least its end plus the deadline (time) or it holds N decided entries, and only a closed window is judged. The binomial tails are summed in log space in Float (n up to 20000) and compared with 1 - confidence."
