      "LeanFM.Session.Types defines Ty (nat, int, str, bool, msg name, list, opt), Field, Message (name, fields, doc) and Env. Text.file reads structure Name [where fields] [deriving ...] before the first protocol into St.types (fieldType reads a plain name or List/Array/Option of one; grouped names x y : T; the doc comment in the gap before the structure becomes Message.doc), and Text.parse runs Types.check (names, keywords, duplicates, nesting, references, Types.ordered for cycles, limits) and then Types.checkCondition on every condition of every protocol with that protocol's idLabels: Where.parse, then typeOf, which resolves each path with Types.leaf (refusing lists, whole structures and _secr names) and checks operand types, and requires bool. renameIds re-renders a copied condition with Where.Expr.mapIds so copies of a bounded loop read their own ids; Expr.render parenthesizes nested operations so it parses back. Parsed.types and SessionTools.Protocol.types carry the Env; the JSON form's types go through jsonTypesText, which admits only identifiers, colons and spaces. session_conform calls Types.checkFields on each event. session_types answers Types.proto, Types.lean and Message.schema for Types.complete (declared structures in dependency order plus an empty one per undeclared label). Global.openApi takes the Env and writes Types.complete (only structures reachable from its labels) as closed schemas. pythonSkeleton and typescriptSkeleton write pyMessage dataclasses (sent through _plain, which turns a dataclass into a dict) and tsMessage interfaces, annotate send bodies with Types.protoName of the label, and refuse a message type named like a class of the module (classNames)."
      ["LeanFM/Session/TypesTests.lean: PlaceOrder's structures, fields, types and doc comments are read; a one-line structure with deriving; grouped fields for a game move (Play x y, Pass); nested, List and Option fields; undeclared, cyclic, repeated, keyword, nested-wrapper, built-in, defaulted, late and 65 structures are refused; typed conditions pass and a missing field, mismatched types, a number condition, a whole message, an unknown id, a string compared with a number, an untyped label, a secret, a list and a whole structure are refused with their reasons; copies of a bounded loop type-check; logs with an undeclared field, a wrong type, a negative Nat, a secret, or a field on an empty message are refused; session_types writes proto3 and Lean (dependency order) and closed schemas; OpenAPI's CreateOrder schema is exact; the Python and TypeScript skeletons hold the dataclass and interface and typed send methods; a message named Endpoint is refused; the JSON form's types work and a field carrying protocol text is refused", "LeanFM/Session/WhereTests.lean: the Tier example declares Order; conditions outside the language or about an unknown id are refused at read time", "LeanFM/SessionToolsTests.lean: the reference examples declare their types; the lending skeletons are regenerated from the typed Lending.protocol", "examples/vibecode/lending: Lending.protocol declares Borrow, Hold and Return; lending.py sends the dataclasses; its tests, its log and tsc pass"]
  , decision "session-envelope"
      ["clause:selfhost.session.envelope", "clause:selfhost.session.execution", "clause:selfhost.session.conform", "clause:selfhost.session.skeleton"]
      ["LeanFM/Session/Types.lean", "LeanFM/Session/Text.lean", "LeanFM/SessionTools.lean", "LeanFM/Session/Skeleton.lean", "LeanFM/Session/SkeletonTs.lean", "LeanFM/MCP.lean"]
      "Types.decimal? reads an optional - and 1 to 20 digits; Types.integer? accepts that string, or a whole JSON number within Types.maxSafe (2^53 - 1), and names why otherwise. Types.checkFields accepts integers through integer? and coerceFields turns them into exact numbers before conformance runs conditions. SessionTools.wireNat reads ts, prev, cause and at the same way for session_sla, which also refuses labels outside Global.labels and reward units outside Text.unitsOf (amounts, rates, penalties) and scales each requirement's ms deadline and time window by 10^6, since the stream is in nanoseconds. deadlineReports reads ts (rounding up to ms) when an event has no timeMs. stampNs orders a generated stream by (time, position), waits each event for its prior and cause, and gives ts = max(time x 10^6, previous ts + 1, latest prior ts + 1) as a decimal string; all three session_simulate paths use it and answer tsUnit ns. Text reads sessions by x.field into St.keys, checks x is declared in that block, and Text.parse checks the field with Types.leaf (Nat or String, not _secr); Protocol.keys carries them; conform groups events by session and, for each key, compares the first event with the key's label against its session (keyProblems, a violation). logEvent takes ts as the id when there is no id. Types.proto appends message Event (ts, id, session, from, to, label, cause, prev, oneof payload over the labels' messages) and refuses a message named Event. The Python runtime has SCHEMA and TYPES per message, _encode/_to_wire (integers to decimal strings, types checked, dicts built into their dataclass) on send and _decode/_from_wire (decimal strings or safe numbers, unknown and missing fields refused) in Endpoint.received, which returns the message with its typed body; _now_ns stamps ts from a replaceable clock (set_clock) strictly increasing. The TypeScript runtime does the same with encode/decode, bigint for Nat and Int, nowNs and setClock, and receive's union carries body typed by label. A message with fields has a required body parameter; one without, an optional one. conditionReads and readsLiteral take the keys so the key field is logged."
      ["LeanFM/Session/EnvelopeTests.lean: untimed, timed and chain streams are stamped with distinct ns ts after their prior and cause events, and session-relative times repeat while ts do not; stampNs separates equal times and waits for priors; a keyed protocol conforms when sessions name the key's value, violates naming the value otherwise and when the key is not logged; a Nat key past 2^64 - 1 compares exactly; READS holds the key; a key outside its block, a Bool key, a secret key and a missing field are refused; the proto has Event with ts and a oneof over the messages; a message named Event is refused", "LeanFM/Session/TypesTests.lean: decimal-string integers conform, are exact past 2^53 (9007199254740993 against ...992 violates), and a number past 2^53 or with a fraction is refused; required and optional body parameters", "LeanFM/Session/SlaTests.lean: the stream is in nanoseconds (299999999 ns hits a 300 ms deadline, 300000001 misses); ts as a decimal string past 2^53 works; a number past 2^53 and a fraction are refused; an unknown label and an unknown reward unit are refused", "examples/vibecode/lending/test_lending.py: received bodies are dataclasses; a body with an extra or wrongly typed field is refused on send and on receive; integers encode to decimal strings and a number past 2^53 is refused; ts are unique, increasing and past 10^18; the checked-in logs replay with set_clock", "examples/vibecode/lending/typestate_errors.ts: a Hold without its book, or with a field it does not have, does not type-check", "protoc compiled the generated place_order.proto and lending.proto while this was written"]
