      ["LeanFM/Session/Syntax.lean", "LeanFM/Session/Global.lean", "LeanFM/Session/Text.lean", "LeanFM/SessionTools.lean", "projects/GoServer/spec/SessionPanel.lean", "examples/sessions", "examples/oauth/SessionType.leanfm", "examples/vibecode", "book/generated/legal-session-inference"]
      "LeanFM/Session/Syntax.lean declares the sess_stmt category with one named syntax per construct (sessMsg, sessEvent, sessChoice, sessDeclared, sessPar, sessJoin, sessRec, sessBounded, sessSessions, sessKeyed, sessCont, sessInclude, sessClock, sessObligation, sessAccrue) and abbreviations for fractions, durations, delays, time references and expressions, quantities, amounts and rates; every construct word is non-reserved except require, whose command needs a leading token, and time(, which the tokenizer reads whole. Conditions: the sess_cond category holds the symbol operators by precedence; the words and and or join operands in two looser layers (sess_conj, sess_where), because Lean does not try a non-reserved word as a trailing operator; condTerm and whereTerm turn a condition into Or, And, Not, Eq, Ne, LT.lt, LE.le, GT.gt, GE.ge and the arithmetic classes, and the message rule elaborates fun (x : Label) ... => decide (prop) over the ids the condition mentions, kept as an unused let beside the Guard, whose only field is now its text (the Dynamic payload evaluator is gone: conformance runs the text with Session.Where). condText keeps the source text with whitespace runs single, and for a renamed copy writes Where.parse of the renamed text rendered, as Text.renameIds does. Bounded loops: unroll works on the syntax as Text.unroll works on statements: inner loops first, copy k renames the body's declared ids with suffix _k (ids, causes, conditions and time references), and splice replaces the continue that ends a block with the next copy or the otherwise block. Annotations, clocks, obligations and accruals expand to nothing; a declared choice is Global.choice through declaredChoice. The protocol command is an elab_rules: it refuses repeated roles and a label equal to the protocol name, declares structure L for each label that resolves to no constant, then elaborates def Name {R} (roles : R) : Global R := sess% [] { ... }. require per q { ... } elaborates to nothing. Text.file skips the import header without consuming the following doc comment; Text.parse refuses a protocol whose body has a label of its name and any protocol, role, label or message id in leanWords; Text.header is written first by writeAll and by the JSON echo; SessionPanel writes it first in goserver.leanfm. Types.reserved adds Lean's keywords so a field name is a Lean field name."
      ["LeanFM/Session/LeanSyntaxTests.lean: #elab_leanfm parses each file's header (it must import LeanFM.Session.Syntax and only loaded modules) and elaborates every command in a namespace of its own with errors at the file's lines: the 13 examples/sessions files, examples/oauth/SessionType.leanfm, the six examples/vibecode protocols, exports/nested-splits/Nested.leanfm, the three book/generated/legal-session-inference files and GoServer's goserver.leanfm all elaborate; PlaceOrder, PingServer, BoundedRide, DepositSettlement, RentWithRepairs, Loan, UserLookup, SignIn, Lending and Trip-parallel agree with the text reading; an undeclared label is an empty structure and a declared one keeps its fields; a bounded loop's copies carry ids t and t_2, causes and conditions as the text reading writes them; a JSON protocol's echoed text and PlaceOrder and BoundedRide written back by writeAll elaborate (#elab_leanfm_text) and agree; negative: a missing field, an unbound id, a protocol named like its label and repeated roles are errors (#guard_msgs), statements holding function application or a tactic do not parse, and the text reading refuses the name clash and keyword names and reads past the header keeping the doc comment", "LeanFM/Session/SessionTests.lean: the purchase's guard keeps its text", "lake env lean on each session-type file elaborates it standalone"]
