      ["LeanFM/Session/Conform.lean"]
      "Global.conforms checks a session against the top-level body and, if it does not fit, against each body Global.nestedSessions lists, keeping the first that fits (else the top-level result). LeanFM/Session/Conform.lean: Global.conforms groups the log by session and runs Conform.checkSession on each against the body of a top-level sessions block or the whole protocol. A State is a residual global type with the protocol message ids bound to event ids; Conform.step is the derivative of a global type by one event: msg and act match label, roles and (unless ignoreCause) the event bound to the protocol's cause; choice tries every branch; par and join move one branch at a time, par continues when every branch can end and join k continues as a par of the continuation and the unfinished branches; loop unfolds by Conform.subst with fuel 64; box is inlined with Global.andThen; nested sessions belong to other session ids. States are deduplicated by a text key (Conform.key) and capped at 512. Conform.nullable decides whether a state can end; Conform.heads lists what a state allows next for the messages. checkSession reports a repeated id, a cause that is not an earlier event, an event no state allows (with heads, and a note when it fits apart from its cause), the cap, and an early stop unless allowIncomplete. Global.mapRoles maps a typed protocol to role names. Global.next runs Conform.statesAfter (checkSession, then the states after each event) and collects Conform.nextOf of every state: the heads of the residual global type with each cause looked up in the state's bindings, and Conform.nullable for whether the session may end."
